{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/422464-crossover-questions-dealing-with-mummies-and-mages-please-answer-if-you-can","id":422464,"title":"Crossover questions dealing with mummies and mages. Please answer if you can.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-27T19:24:05-08:00","id":422464,"title":"Crossover questions dealing with mummies and mages. Please answer if you can.","content":"1. Is Duat in the Underworld or its own plane of existance?<br /> 2. If it is in the underworld could a Giest/Mage get to the gates?<br /> 3. If a mage could get their hands on the ritual to create a Mummy what would happen to the soul and would they even be allowed through the gates to be judged? <br /> 4. While a mummy is not in their body, could a mage use a summon ghost spell to bring the mummy to them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2448-dante","name":"Dante","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T19:37:46-08:00","id":422485,"title":"","content":"1. The latter.<br /> 3. The Rite of Return literally cannot be replicated anymore, so at best you'd have a weird curiosity on your hands to study.<br /> 4. They're Deathless, so probably not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T19:49:17-08:00","id":422493,"title":"","content":"1) Most likely it's own, though it has been theorized by some to be the 'Surface' of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> 2) IF it is, then theoretically yes. But we don't know for sure.<br /> <br /> 3) The mage would probably be unable to perform the ritual on their own for a number of reasons including; not having the resources of a country with specific infrastructure (or Infrastructure) for that kind of magical endeavour, being a non-Supernal rite that requires interactions between the Realms which would require archmastery, not having a kingdom to sacrifice, the flows of energy that is less easily tracked by Supernal magic tend to be overwhelmed/dispersed when directly influence by other forms of magic...<br /> Plus, at no point in time did any of those who conducted the rite know all the secrets behind it. Certainly the entirety of it was never recorded in one place.<br /> <br /> 4)...I'm not sure. I'm inclined to say no in regards to the Arisen (with the Deceived being a special exception) but if Duat is a part of the Underworld then perhaps it can be done. I would require a higher dot rating though, as their souls are bound more tightly to this other plane of existence &amp; other forces are interacting with them. Maybe a requisite dot or 2 from Spirit &amp; Fate...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T02:19:08-08:00","id":422730,"title":"","content":"1. Duat isn't in the Underworld (Mummy calls Duat &quot;the underworld&quot; in a few places, but that's like vampire's astral travel not sending them to the Astral Realms. Who are you to say they can't use the word? Get off their backs.)<br /> <br /> 2. See above.<br /> <br /> 3. They can't.<br /> <br /> 4. No. Arisen are not ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T08:49:20-08:00","id":422975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/422464-crossover-questions-dealing-with-mummies-and-mages-please-answer-if-you-can?p=422730#post422730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. They can't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Is it because Mages can't become Arisen? Or because Mages can't perform the Rite of Return? Or because the Rite could've been done only by the Shan'iatu and only under very special surcumstances?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/120-daimon","name":"Daimon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T10:27:16-08:00","id":423090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daimon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/422464-crossover-questions-dealing-with-mummies-and-mages-please-answer-if-you-can?p=422975#post422975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why? Is it because Mages can't become Arisen? Or because Mages can't perform the Rite of Return? Or because the Rite could've been done only by the Shan'iatu and only under very special surcumstances?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Rite has never been duplicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T12:27:20-08:00","id":423304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/422464-crossover-questions-dealing-with-mummies-and-mages-please-answer-if-you-can?p=422730#post422730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Duat isn't in the Underworld (Mummy calls Duat &quot;the underworld&quot; in a few places, but that's like vampire's astral travel not sending them to the Astral Realms. Who are you to say they can't use the word? Get off their backs.)<br /> <br /> 2. See above.<br /> <br /> 3. They can't.<br /> <br /> 4. No. Arisen are not ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of this is correct. Expanding a bit on #3, each of the game lines have an intended &quot;specialness&quot; to them in which one line does not co-opt another. It would be as inappropriate for mages to make mummies as it would be for mummies to have an utterance that awakens mortals as mages. Even more importantly, it is a key part of mummy that the Rite is something miraculous from a bygone age of epic sorcery, something that happened once and transformed the world and then has never (and could never) be duplicated without very extensive changes to the setting. Mummies are living relics (literally) of antiquity, rooted in a glorious past that has decayed until its traces barely remain. This is part of their tragedy, especially since the decline of Memory means they have personally decayed and lost their past even right along with the other legacies of Irem. They must struggle to hold onto the pieces of who they were and expend enormous effort to probe the mysteries of where they came from.<br /> <br /> This is not to say that you are having badwrong fun if you want to tell a story of modern mystics making their own mummies, only that canon has strong reasons not to permit that within official material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T14:16:32-08:00","id":423434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/422464-crossover-questions-dealing-with-mummies-and-mages-please-answer-if-you-can?p=423090#post423090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Rite has never been duplicated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd put money on a table the first Mekhet (the ones who don't have brains in their own skulls because they were mummified) and Nepri were failed OLLLLLLLLD Kingdom Egypt attempts at just that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T19:20:04-08:00","id":423708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/422464-crossover-questions-dealing-with-mummies-and-mages-please-answer-if-you-can?p=423434#post423434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd put money on a table the first Mekhet (the ones who don't have brains in their own skulls because they were mummified) and Nepri were failed OLLLLLLLLD Kingdom Egypt attempts at just that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure Mummy's cleopatra's egypt will be giving LOTS of hints in it's crossover sidebar.<br /> <br /> Which, all things considered, there was a very Roman flavor to this kickstarter.<br /> <br /> You got Forsaken by Rome, and you got Cleopatra's Egypt (which again, was knocked over by Rome).<br /> <br /> So you got Vampire, Mummy, and Werewolf gamelines all within the roughly the same era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T23:38:36-08:00","id":423879,"title":"","content":"...why is this a bad thing?<br /> <br /> Aside from the opportunity cost?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T08:40:51-08:00","id":424183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/422464-crossover-questions-dealing-with-mummies-and-mages-please-answer-if-you-can?p=423879#post423879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...why is this a bad thing?<br /> <br /> Aside from the opportunity cost?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is what a bad thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T10:29:42-08:00","id":424291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/422464-crossover-questions-dealing-with-mummies-and-mages-please-answer-if-you-can?p=424183#post424183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why is what a bad thing?</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So you got Vampire, Mummy, and Werewolf gamelines all within the roughly the same era. </div> </div> </div>Took me a bit of a staring session as well to sort it out.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:37:32-08:00","id":424434,"title":"","content":"Still don't get it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:51:45-08:00","id":424444,"title":"","content":"Oh, nor I; I only managed to parse what was being referred to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:52:26-08:00","id":424447,"title":"","content":"I think it's important to remember that Mages are really Supernal weavers and that the Fallen World has a lot of magic itself unrelated to this. The Rite of Return wasn't accomplished by playing with the symbols of the world, so a Mage wouldn't immediately have access to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:57:32-08:00","id":424462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/422464-crossover-questions-dealing-with-mummies-and-mages-please-answer-if-you-can?p=424444#post424444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, nor I; I only managed to parse what was being referred to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he was referring to the idea to idea that instead of a few eras overlapping with Rome, they should've been more spread out.<br /> <br /> I think.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T15:10:52-08:00","id":424587,"title":"","content":"Here's my question inspired by &quot;To the Strongest&quot; and the possibility of an Egyptian Cult writeup if it gets expanded: How able are Mages to tell that Irem, its relics, ruins, signs &amp; entities are &quot;not theirs&quot; - given that Mages across cultures have a sense of a lost civilization beyond the reach of time, and here are remains of a destroyed civilization ruled by sorcerers before all of known history - it would seem an easy mistake to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T15:27:45-08:00","id":424600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/422464-crossover-questions-dealing-with-mummies-and-mages-please-answer-if-you-can?p=424587#post424587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's my question inspired by &amp;quot;To the Strongest&amp;quot; and the possibility of an Egyptian Cult writeup if it gets expanded: How able are Mages to tell that Irem, its relics, ruins, signs &amp; entities are &amp;quot;not theirs&amp;quot; - given that Mages across cultures have a sense of a lost civilization beyond the reach of time, and here are remains of a destroyed civilization ruled by sorcerers before all of known history - it would seem an easy mistake to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that brings up the question of how Prime relates to Sekhem. Or Pyros, for that matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T19:58:47-08:00","id":424791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/422464-crossover-questions-dealing-with-mummies-and-mages-please-answer-if-you-can?p=424600#post424600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess that brings up the question of how Prime relates to Sekhem. Or Pyros, for that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess is that there are things related to the Supernal found in the various bits of different versions of Atlantis/Lemuria/Shambala. I never purchased the 1e book so I don't know what it says.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T07:29:44-08:00","id":425163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/422464-crossover-questions-dealing-with-mummies-and-mages-please-answer-if-you-can?p=423434#post423434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd put money on a table the first Mekhet (the ones who don't have brains in their own skulls because they were mummified) and Nepri were failed OLLLLLLLLD Kingdom Egypt attempts at just that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I mentioned it when mummy first started rolling out, but I think it would be amusing to have a Meret run afoul of vampires a few times and each time tell one of them that the shadowy vampires seem familiar for some reason.<br /> <br /> Raise memory high enough and suddenly &quot;hey, remember that pet project that turned out to be a *really bad idea*?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T20:11:41-08:00","id":428469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/422464-crossover-questions-dealing-with-mummies-and-mages-please-answer-if-you-can?p=424600#post424600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that brings up the question of how Prime relates to Sekhem. Or Pyros, for that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>doesn\u2019t</i> relate to Pyros, even though it would make a lot of sense if it did. It\u2019s one of those bits of weirdness about the nWoD: even though the imagery of the Aether <i>seems</i> like it would be a good fit for the Divine Fire and the <i>qashmallim</i>, it turns out that it\u2019s not connected. <br /> <br /> As for Sekhem, my guess is that it\u2019s more of a Life-and-Death thing, though it may be more complex than that. Certainly, if I were to try to associate Arcana with elements of Arisen metaphysics, I\u2019d be more inclined to start with the Pillars: five Pillars, five Paths and five Subtle Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T20:34:17-08:00","id":428508,"title":"","content":"At least as far as Sekhem goes, it should be a 'polluted' mixture. Something that would not naturally occur in the Supernal Realms, as it is 'native' to the Fallen World.<br /> Seeing as how Sekhem has been described as life-force, memories &amp; fate at different points then if I must make a stab I'd say it relates to Life, Mind &amp; Fate jumbled up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T17:53:06-07:00","id":442015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/422464-crossover-questions-dealing-with-mummies-and-mages-please-answer-if-you-can?p=424600#post424600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess that brings up the question of how Prime relates to Sekhem. Or Pyros, for that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought that Pyros (and the Principle, for that matter), was what made up the Empyreal, and because it's super-abstract &quot;big-T Truth&quot;, it's beyond the ken of even Supernal Magic.<br /> <br /> As far as the Rite of Return, it actually seems to resemble an inversion of how humanity used to be in the never-was past of Atlantis. Perhaps the Rite was some perversion of the natural order that managed to survive being time-erased by specifically turning away from the Supernal. If I'm even remotely making sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T21:01:07-07:00","id":442143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/422464-crossover-questions-dealing-with-mummies-and-mages-please-answer-if-you-can?p=442015#post442015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as the Rite of Return, it actually seems to resemble an inversion of how humanity used to be in the never-was past of Atlantis. Perhaps the Rite was some perversion of the natural order that managed to survive being time-erased by specifically turning away from the Supernal. If I'm even remotely making sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more or less how I see it. To use Plato's analogy, they retreated even deeper into the cave to the point that none of the light from outside could reach them at all and so weren't affected by the changing shadows. Duat was so far away from the Supernal that it couldn't even affect Duat at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T00:50:51-07:00","id":442288,"title":"","content":"My vision of the Rite of Return was it was like a hand reaching through the Fallen World to borrow the Mage term going back impossibly to &quot;before' the universe began.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T09:14:27-07:00","id":442615,"title":"","content":"It should probably be said that the whole &quot;impossible to replicate in the modern day&quot; is no reason to not run a game where mages <i>try</i> to replicate it and everything goes horribly wrong. That sounds like a barrel of fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T19:07:49-07:00","id":443540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/422464-crossover-questions-dealing-with-mummies-and-mages-please-answer-if-you-can?p=442615#post442615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should probably be said that the whole &quot;impossible to replicate in the modern day&quot; is no reason to not run a game where mages <i>try</i> to replicate it and everything goes horribly wrong. That sounds like a barrel of fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Or even goes Horribly Right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T10:42:08-07:00","id":444529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/422464-crossover-questions-dealing-with-mummies-and-mages-please-answer-if-you-can?p=443540#post443540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Or even goes Horribly Right.</div> </div> </div> </div>You violated time. Again. Congratulations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T12:06:19-07:00","id":444655,"title":"","content":"Maybe things went horribly wrong to begin with. Let's see some unexpected side-effects of the Rite of Return:<ul><li>Mummies are <i>not</i> perfectly obedient, and have the Memory trait</li> <li>They awaken seemingly by Fate's decree during Sothic turns with no first purpose - surely something unintended by the Ritualists</li> <li>Cults may summon them and give a Mummy their own purpose</li> <li><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">They can rebuild their souls (Pillars), making Apotheosis is possible</div></div> </div> </div></li> <li><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Shuankhsen were the price they paid to Ammut, who taught them the Rite anyway and is the reason why the Arisen can devolve into Shuankhsen to begin with</div></div> </div> </div></li> <li><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">In the eyes of the Sixth Guild's temakhs, the whole betrayal thing was seen as an unexpected side-effect</div></div> </div> </div></li> <li>They can learn Utterances, a secret ripped from the fabric of the cosmos</li> </ul>Of course, maybe some of this <i>was</i> intended but the core book implies some of these things were definitely unforeseen. So let's play pretend for a moment and think, &quot;Damn, if all this stuff was the Rite gone horribly wrong then what would it be like had it gone horribly right?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T13:34:45-07:00","id":444843,"title":"","content":"...mindless, slavishly-loyal immortal demigod robot servants?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value